// An import in a file of a folder module that is not its designated file.
// second.cone, which the folder sweeps in, and sub/third.cone, in an
// organisational subfolder that joins this module, have no 'mod' line, as such
// files must not, so they have no place for an import: a module's imports come
// right after its 'mod' line, all of them in its designated file [Jon 23 Sep].
// Each import there is refused wherever in the file it is written, and is still
// made, so nothing else is reported. A 'use' in such a file is accepted
// (module_header).
//
// Parse stage, which is why it is its own scenario.

mod module_header_reject;

fn designated() i64 {
  1i64;
}
